      "role": "user",
      "content": "that's hitting the exact tone i was looking for. it really drives home the point that apathy is a choice with consequences. i'm curious though, when you say \"choosing not to see the light,\" do you think that's a fair way to describe the argument that some people stay home because they feel the entire system is fundamentally broken or rigged? or is that just an excuse?",
